Z||000013||mrfixit58||04-07-2001||12:58 PM||||Actually, the bell cracked because the mixture of brass, iron, and tin were not correct. The combination of metals were used to give the bell it's strength and flexibility. If you got the mixture right, the tone would be clear. <P>The bell was cast in England and shipped to the colonies. When the bell was rung, the tone was off so, consiquently, the bell didn't last too long before it developled a crack. The bell was then removed from the tower melted down more tin was added and then re-cast. Unfortunatly, the mix was still off. <P>Unfortunatly, I can't remember how long before the second crack developed.<P>Test later,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
